# Release signing for Otium.
#
# Copy this file to keystore.properties in the repository root and fill in the values.
# keystore.properties is git-ignored, and so are *.jks and *.keystore. Never commit either.
#
# What it does
#   app/build.gradle.kts reads this file and signs release builds with your upload key.
#   Without it, release builds are signed with the debug key and Gradle prints a warning. That
#   build is fine for testing R8 (CI works this way) but Play rejects it.
#
# 1. Create the upload key (once)
#   keytool does not create folders, so make one first. Keep it outside the repository.
#
#     mkdir -p ~/.keys && chmod 700 ~/.keys
#     keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore ~/.keys/otium-release.jks -alias upload \
#       -keyalg RSA -keysize 4096 -validity 10000
#     chmod 600 ~/.keys/otium-release.jks
#
#   Run it in your own terminal so the passwords are not recorded anywhere else.
#   If you leave the key password empty at the prompt, it equals the store password.
#
# 2. Back it up now
#   Store the .jks file and both passwords in a password manager or other offline storage.
#   With Play App Signing on, Google holds the app signing key and a lost upload key can be
#   reset through Play support (it takes days). Without it, a lost key means no more updates.
#
# 3. Register its SHA-1 for Drive sign-in
#
#     keytool -list -v -keystore ~/.keys/otium-release.jks -alias upload
#
#   In Google Cloud (Google Auth Platform, Clients), create an Android OAuth client with package
#   name app.otium and this SHA-1. Each signing certificate needs its own client:
#     - debug key        ~/.android/debug.keystore, alias androiddebugkey, password android
#     - upload key       this keystore (local release builds)
#     - Play app signing Play Console, Test and release, App integrity (installs from Play)
#   A missing client makes the Drive consent fail with DEVELOPER_ERROR.
#
# 4. Fill in the values below
#   storeFile    Absolute path, or relative to the repository root. Gradle does not expand ~,
#                so write /Users/<you>/.keys/otium-release.jks rather than ~/.keys/...
#   keyAlias     The -alias given to keytool.
#   Every key is required; a missing or blank one fails the build with its name.
#
# 5. Check it
#
#     ./gradlew assembleRelease
#     $ANDROID_HOME/build-tools/<version>/apksigner verify --print-certs \
#       app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk
#
#   No "signed with the debug key" warning, and the printed SHA-1 matches step 3.
#
storeFile=/Users/you/.keys/otium-release.jks
storePassword=change-me
keyAlias=upload
keyPassword=change-me
